OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F302A1785242915
OL,3,CMajor earthquake strikes southern Japan
OL,5,FJapan's Prime Minister Sanae Takaichi
OL,6,Fsaid her government had set up a task
OL,7,Fforce across the country to gather
OL,8,Finformation, assess possible damage
OL,9,Fand prepare for rescue operations if
OL,10,Fneeded.
OL,12,FSpeaking to reporters, Takaichi said
OL,13,Fthere had been reports of injuries and
OL,14,Fdamage to roads, bridges and
OL,15,Fbuildings, as well as power outages
OL,16,Fand fires, although the full extent of
OL,17,Fthe impact remained unclear.
OL,19,FShe urged people cooking to take extra
OL,20,Fcare with flames and warned residents
OL,21,Fto be cautious around broken glass.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/8
